  "findings": [
    "HEVC compositor -> encoded matches S2 under the same load (1.75-1.78 vs 1.78 ms p50; ~4.3 ms p99 for both) and S2's quiet-GPU result (1.72 ms p50).",
    "Nearly all of the time is waiting for NVENC; mapping and submitting take <0.1 ms. Under heavy load from another process the wait grows by ~2 ms for every codec, consistent with NVENC's RGB->YUV CUDA kernel waiting for GPU time.",
    "Chrome paces itself to wp_presentation feedback: with feedback at 60 Hz it drew 60 fps despite 240 Hz frame callbacks; with feedback every 240 Hz tick it draws 238-240 fps.",
    "A high-priority EGL context hint (EGL_IMG_context_priority) moved nothing measurable and was reverted."
